        "summary": "A new topological helper orders the closure by Kahn's algorithm with a min-heap on local D-number, so a premise's replacement always exists before any dependent of it is rewired. `_depends_on_closure` keeps its old contract for `--keep-dependents`, which has no defect and whose public arrays must not churn - the separation is two helpers, not a re-sort. Ties break on ascending D-number so the emitted arrays stay reproducible.",
        "taskIds": [
